<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="d42cf7bb">&lt;p&gt;
    Once stakeholders have been identified, it is important to develop appropriate strategies to manage and engage them.
    Engaging the stakeholders helps to build a two way dialogue between the program and stakeholders, enabling them to
    voice concerns and issues and enabling the practitioner to address them in a timely manner.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    First, develop a &amp;nbsp;stakeholder engagement plan:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Based on the stakeholder analysis conducted, develop an engagement plan for each stakeholder segment, which should
        include: 
        &lt;ul&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Objectives for engaging with each stakeholder segment
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Agreed actions for continued stakeholder engagement and communication
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Type of communication channel to be deployed for continued engagement
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Frequency of engagement and communication
            &lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;li&gt;
                Timelines and duration of engagement and communication
            &lt;/li&gt;
        &lt;/ul&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Discuss and validate the stakeholder engagement plan with key program team members and program leadership members
        (if required)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Agree stakeholder relationship owners
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop program-wide diversity&amp;nbsp;and inclusiveness approach so that engagement and communication activities are
        tailored to the cultural and demographic mix of the stakeholder landscape
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Then, develop feedback mechanisms:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify stakeholder engagement and communications feedback channels to enable two-way engagement between the
        program and the impacted stakeholder groups
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determine the effectiveness of existing feedback mechanisms
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Develop new feedback mechanisms (if required)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify the process for how feedback will be requested, received, analyzed and fed back into the Business
        Engagement team
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Afterwards, conduct on-going and targeted stakeholder engagement
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identify new stakeholders for the High Level Design and conduct stakeholder analysis and mapping
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Monitor stakeholder engagement activities and update stakeholder engagement plan (as required)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Apply the program-wide diversity&amp;nbsp;and inclusiveness approach so that engagement and communication activities
        are tailored to the cultural and demographic mix of the stakeholder landscape&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
